        ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x) &= \\left(3 x^{3} + 4 x^{2} + 2\\right)^{\\prime} \\\\ &= (3)\\cdot(3)\\cdot x^{2}+(4)\\cdot(2)\\cdot x^{1}+0 \\\\ &= 9 x^{2} + 8 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime\\prime}(x) &= \\left(9 x^{2} + 8 x\\right)^{\\prime} \\\\ &= (9)\\cdot(2)\\cdot x^{1}+(8)\\cdot(1)\\cdot x^{0} \\\\ &= 18 x + 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=-1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime\\prime}(-1) &= 18 (-1) + 8 \\\\ &= -10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
