        ":question/problem": "Find $g^{\\prime\\prime}(1)$ if $g(x)=-2x^{3}+8x\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n$g^{\\prime\\prime}(1)=$ {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g^{\\prime}(x) &= \\left(-2x^{3}+8x\\sqrt{x}\\right)^{\\prime} \\\\ &= \\left(8x^{3/2}-2x^{3}\\right)^{\\prime} \\\\ &= (8)\\cdot(\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot x^{1/2}+(-2)\\cdot(3)\\cdot x^{2} \\\\ &= 12 \\sqrt{x} - 6 x^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g^{\\prime\\prime}(x) &= \\left(12 \\sqrt{x} - 6 x^{2}\\right)^{\\prime} \\\\ &= (12)\\cdot(\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot x^{-1/2}+(-6)\\cdot(2)\\cdot x^{1} \\\\ &= - 12 x + \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g^{\\prime\\prime}(1) &= - 12 (1) + \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{(1)}} \\\\ &= -6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
